=== Setsusha ===

=== Sessha ===
There are four Setsusha shrines.<ref>The description of Setsusha shrines is based on the Shrine History Book. </ref>. Both shrines are enshrined along the Hakuunbashi course in Mt. Tsukuba, and enshrine the {{ill|lt=mikogami|Q352176|WD=Q352176|1=Mikogami}} ({{ill|lt=Mikiko|Q4702904|WD=Q4702904|1=Three Noble Children}} and Ebisu no Mikoto) of Izanagison and Izashoson.

* Inamura Shrine ({{Coord|36|13|27.5|N|140|6|41.6|E|region:JP-08|name=Inamura Shrine}})
*:* Deity enshrined: {{ill|lt=Amaterasu Omikami|Q455602|WD=Q455602|lt=Amaterasu Omikami|1=Amaterasu}} (Amaterasu Omikami)
*: It is enshrined on a huge stone at the end of Benkei Seven Return. This megalith is also called "{{ill|lt=Takamagahara|Q1141974|WD=Q1141974|1=Takamagahara}}".
* Azatsune Shrine ({{Coord|36|13|28.5|N|140|6|26|E|region:JP-08|name=Azatsune Shrine}})
*:* Enshrined deity: {{ill|lt=Susanoo|Q272993|WD=Q272993|lt=Susanoo|1=Susanoo-no-Mikoto}} (Susanoo no Mikoto)
*: Enshrined in front of ``Byobu Rock'' beyond ``Hokuto Rock''.
* Koharagi Shrine ({{Coord|36|13|30.3|N|140|6|31.8|E|region:JP-08|name=Obaraki Shrine}})
*:* Enshrined deity: {{ill|WD=Q595520|lt=Tsukuyomi|Q595520|WD=Q595520|WD=Q595520|lt=Tsukuyomi no Mikoto|1=Tsukuyomi-no-Mikoto}}
*: Enshrined under "Hokuto Rock" (based on the legend that {{ill|lt=Kukai|Q222227|WD=Q222227|lt=Kobo Daishi|1=Kūkai}} saw {{ill|lt=Myoken Bodhisattva|Q10960623|WD=Q10960623|1=Myōken}}).* Watari Shrine ({{Coord|36|13|29.8|N|140|6|36.6|E|region:JP-08|name=Watari Shrine}})
*:* Enshrined deity: {{ill|lt=Hiruko|Q1067028|WD=Q1067028|lt=Ebisu no Mikoto|1=Hiruko}} (Hiruko no Mikoto)
*: Enshrined near the strange rock "Uramen Daikoku".

In addition, at the former Rokusho Shrine (Usui, Tsukuba City: Tsukubasan Shrine Motosato Shrine) and Rokusho Shrine (Izumi, Tsukuba City), the ``Rokusho'', which includes the above-mentioned four sessha shrines, was enshrined in addition to the two deities of Tsukuba Men and Women.

