** Parking lots cost around 500 yen for direct, public, and private parking lots. However, you can use the paid parking lot at Tsukubasanjinja Shrine for free for one hour. </ref>. The farthest Tsukuba Municipal Parking Lot No. 1 is open for free (except during the Mt. Tsukuba plum grove season), but it requires a long walk along a busy prefectural road.For information on climbing to the main shrine of Mt. Nantai and Mt. Nyotai, see "{{ill|lt=Mt. Tsukuba #climbing|Q1754619|WD=Q1754619|1=Mount Tsukuba}}".

